  reading the numbers:
   - ingestion writes go to ONE SQLite storage: if the speed-up is well below 2, storage is the
     bottleneck (compare 'storage writes/s' and storage p95 in evidence/scale/2-ingestion-*)
   - analytics only reads, so it should scale better until storage reads saturate
   - the registry is in memory: lookups stay fast, but /services without a filter grows
     linearly and the health checker pings every instance one by one (O(N) per sweep)
   - all instances run on one physical host (on k3s: two k3s nodes = two Incus containers
     on it), so 'dc2' is a logical location: absolute
     numbers are lower bounds, the trends are what matters

